{
  "category": "Licking Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its tongue can be extended like a chameleon's. It leaves a tingling sensation when it licks enemies.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tongue can be extended like a chameleon's. It leaves a tingling sensation when it licks enemies.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tongue spans almost 7 feet and moves more freely than its forelegs. Its licks can cause paralysis.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tongue has well-developed nerves that run to the very tip, so it can be deftly manipulated.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long tongue, slathered with a gooey saliva, sticks to anything, so it is very useful.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has a tongue that is over 6’6’’ long. It uses this long tongue to lick its body clean.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whenever LICKITUNG comes across something new, it will unfailingly give it a lick. It does so because it memorizes things by texture and by taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whenever LICKITUNG comes across something new, it will unfailingly give it a lick. It does so because it memorizes things by texture and by taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whenever it sees something unfamiliar, it always licks the object because it memorizes things by texture and taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tongue is twice the length of its body. It can be moved like an arm for grabbing food and attacking.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tongue can be extended like a chameleon’s. It leaves a tingling sensation when it licks enemies.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of hands, it uses its tongue, which is twice its height. Its sticky saliva grips anything.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of hands, it uses its tongue, which is twice its height. Its sticky saliva grips anything.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it extends its over-six-foot- long tongue, its tail quivers. There is a possibility they are connected.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its tongue has well-developed nerves that run to the very tip, so it can be deftly manipulated.",
